    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 129,
    "end": 133,
    "text": "Compare private and social incentives and identify"
  },
  {
    "start": 134,
    "end": 138,
    "text": "the efficient quantity."
  },
  {
    "start": 139,
    "end": 142,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 143,
    "end": 147,
    "text": "Difficulty:"
  },
  {
    "start": 172,
    "end": 175,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 176,
    "end": 180,
    "text": "Intermediate"
  },
  {
    "start": 182,
    "end": 185,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 186,
    "end": 190,
    "text": "Externalities"
  },
  {
    "start": 200,
    "end": 203,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 204,
    "end": 208,
    "text": "+"
  },
  {
    "start": 210,
    "end": 213,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 214,
    "end": 218,
    "text": "THE CORE IDEA"
  },
  {
    "start": 225,
    "end": 228,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 230,
    "end": 234,
    "text": "An externality is a cost or benefit imposed on someone outside a transaction. Negative externalities make private decision makers"
  },
  {
    "start": 235,
    "end": 239,
    "text": "ignore part of social cost; positive externalities make them ignore part of social benefit. Efficiency uses all marginal social costs and"
  },
  {
    "start": 240,
    "end": 244,
    "text": "benefits."
  },
  {
    "start": 254,
    "end": 257,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 258,
    "end": 262,
    "text": "?"
  },
  {
    "start": 264,
    "end": 267,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 268,
    "end": 272,
    "text": "HOW TO RECOGNIZE IT"
  },
  {
    "start": 279,
    "end": 282,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 283,
    "end": 287,
    "text": "-"
  },
  {
    "start": 288,
    "end": 292,
    "text": "Ask whether the spillover is a cost or benefit and whether it comes from production or consumption."
  },
  {
    "start": 294,
    "end": 297,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 298,
    "end": 302,
    "text": "-"
  },
  {
    "start": 303,
    "end": 307,
    "text": "Negative: MSC > MPC or MPB > MSB, so the market quantity is too high."
  },
  {
    "start": 309,
    "end": 312,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 313,
    "end": 317,
    "text": "-"
  },
  {
    "start": 318,
    "end": 322,
    "text": "Positive: MSB > MPB or MPC > MSC, so the market quantity is too low."
  },
  {
    "start": 324,
    "end": 327,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 328,
    "end": 332,
    "text": "-"
  },
  {
    "start": 333,
    "end": 337,
    "text": "Corrective taxes, subsidies, permits, regulation, or bargaining can internalize the spillover."
  },
  {
    "start": 362,
    "end": 365,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 366,
    "end": 370,
    "text": "!"
  },
  {
    "start": 372,
    "end": 375,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 376,
    "end": 380,
    "text": "WATCH OUT"
  },
  {
    "start": 381,
    "end": 384,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 386,
    "end": 390,
    "text": "Do not label every harmful outcome an externality. A spillover must affect a third party and be missing from the market price."
  },
  {
    "start": 415,
    "end": 418,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 419,
    "end": 423,
    "text": "#"
  },
  {
    "start": 425,
    "end": 428,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 429,
    "end": 433,
    "text": "WORKED EXAMPLE: NEGATIVE PRODUCTION EXTERNALITY"
  },
  {
    "start": 438,
    "end": 441,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 443,
    "end": 447,
    "text": "Fast-fashion production creates a $6 external cost per"
  },
  {
    "start": 448,
    "end": 452,
    "text": "garment, so MSC lies $6 above MPC. The market"
  },
  {
    "start": 453,
    "end": 457,
    "text": "produces 240 million garments where MPB = MPC at"
  },
  {
    "start": 458,
    "end": 462,
    "text": "$12. Efficiency occurs at 160 million garments where"
  },
  {
    "start": 463,
    "end": 467,
    "text": "MPB = MSC at $15, eliminating 80 million units of"
  },
  {
    "start": 468,
    "end": 472,
    "text": "overproduction. A $6 corrective tax aligns private and"
  },
  {
    "start": 473,
    "end": 477,
    "text": "social marginal cost."
  },
  {
    "start": 502,
    "end": 505,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 506,
    "end": 510,
    "text": "?"
  },
  {
    "start": 512,
    "end": 515,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 516,
    "end": 520,
    "text": "CHECK YOURSELF"
  },
  {
    "start": 521,
    "end": 524,
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "start": 526,
    "end": 530,
    "text": "If MSB lies above MPB, is the unregulated market quantity too high or too low?"
  },
